{
 "$schema": "https://json.schemastore.org/sarif-2.1.0.json",
 "version": "2.1.0",
 "runs": [
  {
   "tool": {
    "driver": {
     "name": "CodeQL",
     "organization": "GitHub",
     "semanticVersion": "2.19.3",
     "rules": [
      {
       "id": "js/sql-injection",
       "name": "SqlInjection",
       "shortDescription": {
        "text": "Database query built from user-controlled sources"
       },
       "fullDescription": {
        "text": "Building a database query from user-controlled sources is vulnerable to insertion of malicious code by the user."
       },
       "defaultConfiguration": {
        "level": "error"
       },
       "helpUri": "https://codeql.github.com/codeql-query-help/javascript/js-sql-injection/",
       "help": {
        "text": "Use parameters.",
        "markdown": "# Database query built from user-controlled sources\n\nIf a database query is built from user-provided data without sufficient sanitization, a user may be able to run malicious queries.\n\n## Recommendation\n\nUse **prepared statements** with `?` parameters:\n\n```js\nconn.all(\"SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = ?\", [id]);\n```\n\n## References\n\n- OWASP: [SQL Injection](https://owasp.org/www-community/attacks/SQL_Injection)\n- Common Weakness Enumeration: CWE-89.\n"
       },
       "properties": {
        "tags": [
         "security",
         "external/cwe/cwe-089",
         "external/cwe/cwe-090"
        ],
        "precision": "high",
        "security-severity": "8.8",
        "problem.severity": "error"
       }
      },
      {
       "id": "js/reflected-xss",
       "name": "ReflectedXss",
       "shortDescription": {
        "text": "Reflected cross-site scripting"
       },
       "fullDescription": {
        "text": "Writing user input directly to an HTTP response allows for a cross-site scripting vulnerability."
       },
       "defaultConfiguration": {
        "level": "error"
       },
       "helpUri": "https://codeql.github.com/codeql-query-help/javascript/js-reflected-xss/",
       "help": {
        "text": "Escape output.",
        "markdown": "# Reflected cross-site scripting\n\nDirectly writing user input to a webpage without escaping allows cross-site scripting.\n\n1. Escape the input.\n2. Or use a template engine that escapes by default.\n"
       },
       "properties": {
        "tags": [
         "security",
         "external/cwe/cwe-079",
         "external/cwe/cwe-116"
        ],
        "precision": "high",
        "security-severity": "6.1"
       }
      },
      {
       "id": "js/path-injection",
       "name": "TaintedPath",
       "shortDescription": {
        "text": "Uncontrolled data used in path expression"
       },
       "defaultConfiguration": {
        "level": "error"
       },
       "helpUri": "https://codeql.github.com/codeql-query-help/javascript/js-path-injection/",
       "properties": {
        "tags": [
         "security",
         "external/cwe/cwe-022"
        ],
        "security-severity": "7.5"
       }
      },
      {
       "id": "js/hardcoded-credentials",
       "name": "HardcodedCredentials",
       "shortDescription": {
        "text": "Hard-coded credentials"
       },
       "defaultConfiguration": {
        "level": "warning"
       },
       "properties": {
        "tags": [
         "security",
         "external/cwe/cwe-798"
        ],
        "security-severity": "9.8"
       }
      },
      {
       "id": "js/unused-local-variable",
       "name": "UnusedVariable",
       "shortDescription": {
        "text": "Unused variable, import, function or class"
       },
       "defaultConfiguration": {
        "level": "note"
       },
       "properties": {
        "tags": [
         "maintainability"
        ]
       }
      }
     ]
    }
   },
